From: PW3 Android port
Subject: [PW3] Settings: outlined cards on white

The search bar and the suggestions on the main screen are cards with a 2dp
elevation on a light grey (#f2f2f2) band. On PW3 the shadow is not drawn
(software rendering) and the grey is one panel level below white, so the cards
had no visible edge. As every surface that stands out from the page
(docs/design/eink-ui.md): the band is white, and the cards have no elevation
and a black outline of 1dp (2 px) with corners of 4dp, drawn as their
foreground. Settings' copy of the values is res/values/pw3_eink.xml.

The suggestions card no longer uses compatibility padding: it only made room
for a shadow, and would have put the outline outside the card.

--- /dev/null
+++ b/res/values/pw3_eink.xml
@@ -0,0 +1,9 @@
+<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
+<!-- PW3: the e-paper interface rules (docs/design/eink-ui.md) as Settings uses them. The
+     framework's dialogs, menus and toasts, SystemUI and Launcher3 write the same values. -->
+<resources>
+    <color name="pw3_outline">#ff000000</color>
+    <!-- 2 px on PW3 (density 1.875, rounded to whole pixels). -->
+    <dimen name="pw3_outline_width">1dp</dimen>
+    <dimen name="pw3_corner_radius">4dp</dimen>
+</resources>
--- /dev/null
+++ b/res/drawable/pw3_card_outline.xml
@@ -0,0 +1,8 @@
+<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
+<!-- PW3: a card's edge (docs/design/eink-ui.md), drawn over it as its foreground. The
+     card's shadow is not drawn (software rendering): white on white had no edge. -->
+<shape xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
+       android:shape="rectangle">
+    <stroke android:width="@dimen/pw3_outline_width" android:color="@color/pw3_outline" />
+    <corners android:radius="@dimen/pw3_corner_radius" />
+</shape>
--- a/res/layout/settings_main_dashboard.xml
+++ b/res/layout/settings_main_dashboard.xml
@@ -32,9 +32,10 @@
